# Internal tooling. The repo root is served as the public site, so anything left
# here is fetchable at its own URL. These are excluded from the deployment.
scripts/
.claude/
.githooks/

# Engineering briefs. Same reasoning as the entries above, and it is the reason
# this line was added in the same commit as the directory it excludes: without
# it, docs/briefs/intake-phone.md would have been live at
# neurohome.app/docs/briefs/intake-phone.md — a document that describes an open
# defect, names the file and line it lives at, and explains what it does to a
# parent mid-form. None of that belongs on the public site.
docs/

# robots.txt already carried "Disallow: /compare/", but that only asks crawlers
# not to index it; the page stayed readable to anyone holding the URL. Excluding
# it here is what actually enforces that intent. Nothing links to it and it is not
# in the sitemap. If it turns out to be a page the team sends people to directly,
# delete this line and it is back on the next deploy.
compare/

# Local-only prototypes — not for production
prototype.html
app-preview.html
app-prototype/

# Design-tool bundler exports. Self-unpacking single files that inline their
# own fonts and rewrite the document at runtime. Reference material only, but
# the repo root IS the deploy surface, so an unignored one ships as a live page.
# intake-updated.html in particular carries the real CRM webhooks.
intake-updated.html
NeuroSage Family Section.html
